# Large local-only source assets — stay local, never pushed (see CLAUDE.md)
Blender Files/
GLB Library/*

# ...EXCEPT the two files the ADHESIVE FOOT DERIVATION needs (7.4 kB total).
# Adhesive-Foot.lib.glb is not modelled, it is CUT from the printed foot by
# GLB Pipeline/derive_adhesive_foot.py - so re-exporting the printed master
# silently leaves the derivative wrong, and both files still load and still
# look like feet. `--check` rebuilds the bytes from the master and compares
# them against every shipped copy, which is the only test that can catch a
# stale derivation; without the master in the repo it cannot run in CI, and a
# protection that only runs on one laptop is not a protection on the path that
# reaches users. Everything else under GLB Library/ stays local.
# ⚠ git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so each parent has to be
# re-included before the file can be - the `dir/*` + `!dir/` ladder below is
# that idiom, not redundancy. Deleting any line silently re-ignores the file.
!GLB Library/Hardware/
GLB Library/Hardware/*
!GLB Library/Hardware/Adhesive-Foot.lib.glb
!GLB Library/Hardware/raw/
GLB Library/Hardware/raw/*
!GLB Library/Hardware/raw/Tabletop-Kit-Foot.glb

# gen2_batch.py rewrites this on EVERY run: diagnostic exhaust, not provenance.
# MEASURED on the shelf-insert run - 167 kB, machine-specific absolute paths,
# and 363 canonical_ok rows for a 7-job run because each job rescans everything
# already sitting in its output directory. It also freezes whatever the job
# notes said at run time (that copy still reads "clips up", corrected the same
# day). A real provenance record would need source hashes + tool versions +
# the producing commit, and would be written deliberately, not blessed from this.
GLB Pipeline/run_report.json

# Python bytecode (GLB Pipeline)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local, per-user Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local backup copies (e.g. gen2_jobs.json.bak before a hand-edit)
*.bak

# Render-experiment harness. It lives under viewer/ so the local dev server can
# serve it, which means an untracked file there is one `git add -A` away from
# being DEPLOYED (Pages serves viewer/). It drives the real scene through the
# ?debug=1 hook and ships nothing — keep it that way until we decide otherwise.
viewer/lab/

# Local GoatCounter API token for serve-stats.py — NEVER commit this.
.goatcounter-token
# serve-stats.py's hour baseline (survives restarts so the map pulse doesn't
# cold-start blind) — local business data, stays on this machine
.stats-hour-base.json

# ---- Internal working notes: kept on disk, never published ----
# Session handoffs, batch run logs, calibration notes and the AI project
# memory. They stay in the working tree and keep working exactly as before;
# git simply stops publishing them to a public repo.
CLAUDE.md
GEN2-Part-Orientation-Notes.md
2026-*.md
# Joey's link/catalogue specs. These were sitting UNTRACKED but un-ignored,
# which is a different thing: one `git add -A` would have published them.
GEN2_LINKS_UPDATE_*.md
# AGENTS.md is a COPY of CLAUDE.md for tools that read that filename — same
# private project memory, same rule: on disk, never published.
AGENTS.md
# Archived handoffs and run logs. The patterns above are all basename-only, so
# they keep matching after a move into notes/ — this covers anything else.
notes/

# dependencies (jsdom is a devDependency for the cross-tool parity test only)
node_modules/
package-lock.json
